{"id": "P0", "version": 1, "type": "purpose", "subject": "purpose", "owner": "AU-owner", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "TODO: the owner states what this project is for (stub from aec init)"}
{"id": "P0", "version": 2, "type": "purpose", "subject": "purpose", "owner": "AU-owner", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "QAT-Kit: a modular, human-readable protocol for reflective, composable reasoning: prompt tools (StressTest, TruthWeight and others) that an assistant runs, whose inputs, outputs and handoffs are written as contracts that can be checked rather than merely declared", "rationale": "The repo has no README or purpose file. Taken from Toolkits/Project_Instructions.md L5 (the kit's self-description) and qat/scripts/qat.py L4-9 (why the runner exists: contracts the model might not honour, nothing checking one tool's output fits the next tool's input). docs/ holds only the 2026-11-04 drift inventory and implementation comparison, which describe copies, not purpose. Provisional until Zach states the purpose in his own words; written by kai#telosmith-adoption under DEC-091 (relay-kit-private ledger)", "relations": [{"rel": "supersedes", "to": "P0@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "Toolkits/Project_Instructions.md", "locator": "L5", "for": "text", "sha256": "e54e761725169203e53dd11112a9095604a3f1dabbe33aa7396472177e2e6824"}, {"path": "qat/scripts/qat.py", "locator": "L4-9", "for": "text", "sha256": "2e89f20b135649b15cb5df398b3098878c5405a1aa71ae5fd33f93d50f376dc2"}]}
{"id": "QAT-R-spec", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "Every QAT tool spec (qat/tools/*.qat.md) validates against the spec schema, declares the modules its body uses, and every tool output can be audited against its declared output contract with typed errors (SPEC_INVALID, UNKNOWN_MODULE, MISSING_INPUT, CONTRACT_VIOLATION, TYPE_MISMATCH, UNKNOWN_FIELD)", "rationale": "qat/scripts/qat.py docstring L11-31; the runner never runs a tool, the model does", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}, {"rel": "implemented_by", "to": "code:qat.scripts.qat.validate_spec"}, {"rel": "implemented_by", "to": "code:qat.scripts.qat.audit_output"}], "anchors": [{"path": "qat/scripts/qat.py", "locator": "L11-31", "for": "text", "sha256": "2e89f20b135649b15cb5df398b3098878c5405a1aa71ae5fd33f93d50f376dc2"}]}
{"id": "QAT-R-handoff", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "A declared handoff from one QAT tool to another resolves: the target tool and every mapped field exist and the types coerce; an audited output can be mapped onto the next tool's inputs (BROKEN_HANDOFF otherwise)", "rationale": "qat/scripts/qat.py commands index and handoff (L12, L15)", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}, {"rel": "implemented_by", "to": "code:qat.scripts.qat.check_handoff"}, {"rel": "implemented_by", "to": "code:qat.scripts.qat.build_handoff"}], "anchors": [{"path": "qat/scripts/qat.py", "locator": "L12-15", "for": "text", "sha256": "2e89f20b135649b15cb5df398b3098878c5405a1aa71ae5fd33f93d50f376dc2"}]}
{"id": "QAT-R-eval", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "Each tool with a spec has eval cases (qat/cases/<tool>.eval.yaml) whose deterministic must_include / must_avoid checks the runner scores against saved outputs (EVAL_FAIL otherwise); judge checks are graded by a model and are not deterministic", "rationale": "qat/scripts/qat.py L16; qat/cases/truth-weight.eval.yaml header; first run in qat/eval-runs/2026-11-04/RESULTS.md", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "QAT-R-spec@1"}, {"rel": "implemented_by", "to": "code:qat.scripts.qat.run_eval"}], "anchors": [{"path": "qat/cases/truth-weight.eval.yaml", "locator": "L1-3", "for": "text", "sha256": "c38a83ca14fb75c5a42a51a71eb38ab019db3f4e785afff167db80a8b4fa5571"}]}
{"id": "QAT-D-canon", "version": 1, "type": "decision", "subject": "design", "status": "proposed", "text": "Pointer, not a decision made here: no copy of any QAT tool is canonical yet. DEC-048 (with Kate's amendment) and DEC-051 item 2 in the relay-kit-private ledger record that the drift inventory declares no canonical copy; docs/DRIFT_INVENTORY_2026-11-04.md lists what each copy contains so that a canonical-source recommendation can be made later with evidence. Copying a file into qat/ does not make it canonical (qat/PROVENANCE.md). Records here must not treat qat/tools/*.qat.md as the canonical tool until Zach decides otherwise. Status stays proposed until Zach accepts this record", "rationale": "DEC-091 (relay-kit-private ledger): each adopting repo's records cite the private ledger decisions that govern it", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}], "anchors": [{"path": "docs/DRIFT_INVENTORY_2026-11-04.md", "locator": "q:no copy is declared canonical here.", "for": "text", "sha256": "378007039261aeec9df0b6b58abb455097d777ac4588a9d80bac06976ec4c26b"}, {"path": "qat/PROVENANCE.md", "locator": "q:Copying a file here does not make it canonical.", "for": "text", "sha256": "4cd52131083a06468b85ec23c66c250dc4a54f11a0b76bfdc075c84dc5065fd4"}]}
{"id": "QAT-R-replay", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "A counterbalanced blind replay of a QAT study tool is reproducible from a seed: each grader sees every item exactly once and never the same item in both arms, the two graders see complementary arms balanced within each stratum, grader packets carry opaque ids and never the arm, and the tally joins grades back to arms and lists for the owner only the items where graders split on (or both dispute) the reference key", "rationale": "DEC-158 item 2 (relay-kit-private ledger): evaluate real-problem and kind-check by counterbalanced blind replay, owner adjudicating only disagreements; qat/studies/replay-dec158/README.md; tests in qat/scripts/test_replay.py. Proposed by claude:qat#sub-01GZK2K-qat2, 2026-11-07; provisional until the owner commits it", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "QAT-R-eval@1"}, {"rel": "implemented_by", "to": "code:qat.scripts.replay.assign"}, {"rel": "implemented_by", "to": "code:qat.scripts.replay.split_halves"}, {"rel": "implemented_by", "to": "code:qat.scripts.replay.packet"}, {"rel": "implemented_by", "to": "code:qat.scripts.replay.tally"}]}
{"id": "QAT-R-distill", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "QAT-Kits has a thread-distill tool that compresses a conversation into a layered distillate (hook, abstract, status ledger, ideas, coined terms, open threads, trajectory, compression notes) at hook, brief or full fidelity, readable by the user later, by another model, or by another tool, with every status and attribution traceable to a turn pointer", "rationale": "Zach, 2026-11-05 14:53 CT, to the QAT lane: the most important tool to design and iterate for the moment is one that usefully distills and compresses a thread", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "QAT-R-spec@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "QAT-R-eval@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "qat/tools/thread-distill.qat.md", "locator": "L1-4", "for": "text", "sha256": "84f92df929f2ecc45741230e8f476f0a935830e718ba2c236d300bcead0a46a2"}]}
{"id": "QAT-D-distill-design", "version": 1, "type": "decision", "subject": "design", "status": "proposed", "text": "Design choices for thread-distill as Zach answered them (2026-11-05, QAT lane chat): (1) one distillate serves all readers at a set fidelity; (2) a new spec drawing on ContextAnchor, ThreadMap, MetaDistill, SSD and thread-seed rather than reviving or folding into one of them, with thread-seed later able to consume its output; (3) real test threads are named by Zach and captured outside this public repo, only constructed eval cases are committed; (4) it must run as a Claude skill, in a ChatGPT project and under the qat.py runner. Status stays proposed until Zach accepts this record", "rationale": "Answers to the QAT lane's four design questions; recorded so later iterations do not reopen them", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "QAT-R-distill@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "QAT-D-canon@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "qat/tools/thread-distill.qat.md", "locator": "L1-4", "for": "text", "sha256": "84f92df929f2ecc45741230e8f476f0a935830e718ba2c236d300bcead0a46a2"}]}
{"id": "QAT-R-distill", "version": 2, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "Withdrawn from records: thread-distill is a Kit, and Kits are not governed by Telosmith. Its design provenance now lives in qat/tools/thread-distill.DESIGN.md", "rationale": "Zach, 2026-11-06 11:02 CT (QAT lane): accepted the 2026-11-05 Claude/Kate direction that Telosmith governs only the machinery (runner, spec schema, eval harness, creation pipeline) and not the Kits; tool content and design provenance are Kit-owned (relay-kit-private handoffs/outputs/qat-2026-11-05-telosmith-scope-debate.md)", "relations": [{"rel": "supersedes", "to": "QAT-R-distill@1"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}], "anchors": [{"path": "qat/tools/thread-distill.DESIGN.md", "locator": "L1-3", "for": "rationale", "sha256": "060bc44997da5321fcaa016b56186a85589a6d62b0ac5b2e771c484e2b9884a7"}]}
{"id": "QAT-D-distill-design", "version": 2, "type": "decision", "subject": "design", "status": "proposed", "text": "Withdrawn from records: Zach's four thread-distill design answers moved, unchanged, to qat/tools/thread-distill.DESIGN.md (Kit-owned)", "rationale": "Zach, 2026-11-06 11:02 CT (QAT lane): accepted the 2026-11-05 Claude/Kate direction that Telosmith governs only the machinery (runner, spec schema, eval harness, creation pipeline) and not the Kits; tool content and design provenance are Kit-owned (relay-kit-private handoffs/outputs/qat-2026-11-05-telosmith-scope-debate.md)", "relations": [{"rel": "supersedes", "to": "QAT-D-distill-design@1"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}], "anchors": [{"path": "qat/tools/thread-distill.DESIGN.md", "locator": "L1-3", "for": "rationale", "sha256": "060bc44997da5321fcaa016b56186a85589a6d62b0ac5b2e771c484e2b9884a7"}]}
{"id": "QAT-R-create", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "New QAT tools are created through the repo's machinery: a spec that qat.py validates, an eval stub with constructed fixtures, a blind cold run by an actor who has not seen the evals, and acceptance by Zach; eval results record who wrote each case and whether it was graded deterministically or by a model, and an author's own judge grades stay provisional until independently graded. Telosmith governs this pipeline, not the tools it produces", "rationale": "Zach, 2026-11-06 11:02 CT (QAT lane): accepted the 2026-11-05 Claude/Kate direction that Telosmith governs only the machinery (runner, spec schema, eval harness, creation pipeline) and not the Kits; tool content and design provenance are Kit-owned (relay-kit-private handoffs/outputs/qat-2026-11-05-telosmith-scope-debate.md); Kate's conditions on evaluation provenance and candidate-vs-accepted improvements (same file, round 2, item 5)", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "QAT-R-spec@1"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "QAT-R-eval@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "qat/scripts/qat.py", "locator": "L1-40", "for": "text", "sha256": "2e89f20b135649b15cb5df398b3098878c5405a1aa71ae5fd33f93d50f376dc2"}]}
